     3,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><br>\n<br><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\">On Wed, Apr 18, 2012 at 10:19 AM, Dan Linden <span dir=\"ltr\">&lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">danl...@gmail.com</a>&gt;</span> wrote:<br><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0 0 0 .8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\">\n\nThe following code would identify the poor models (those beyond 95% of the cumulative AIC weight) and set them to NULL in your model list:<br><br><span style=\"text-indent:0px;letter-spacing:normal;font-variant:normal;text-align:auto;font-style:normal;font-weight:normal;line-height:normal;border-collapse:separate;text-transform:none;font-size:medium;white-space:normal;font-family:Arial;word-spacing:0px\"><span style=\"font-family:&#39;Lucida Console&#39;;font-size:16px;line-height:19px;text-align:-webkit-left;white-space:pre-wrap\"><pre style=\"font-family:&#39;Lucida Console&#39;;font-size:12pt!important;outline-style:none;outline-width:initial;outline-color:initial;border-top-style:none;border-right-style:none;border-bottom-style:none;border-left-style:none;border-width:initial;border-color:initial;white-space:pre-wrap!important;margin-top:0px;margin-right:0px;margin-bottom:0px;margin-left:0px;line-height:1.2\">\n\n<span style=\"text-indent:0px;letter-spacing:normal;font-variant:normal;text-align:auto;font-style:normal;font-weight:normal;line-height:normal;border-collapse:separate;text-transform:none;font-size:medium;white-space:normal;font-family:Arial;word-spacing:0px\"><span style=\"font-family:&#39;Lucida Console&#39;;font-size:16px;line-height:19px;text-align:-webkit-left;white-space:pre-wrap\"><pre style=\"font-family:&#39;Lucida Console&#39;;font-size:12pt!important;outline-style:none;outline-width:initial;outline-color:initial;border-top-style:none;border-right-style:none;border-bottom-style:none;border-left-style:none;border-width:initial;border-color:initial;white-space:pre-wrap!important;margin-top:0px;margin-right:0px;margin-bottom:0px;margin-left:0px;line-height:1.2\">\n\n<span style=\"color:blue\">poor.models &lt;- </span><span style=\"color:blue\">modSel.object@Full$model[</span><span style=\"color:blue\">which(modSel.object@Full$cumltvWt&gt;0.95),]</span><span style=\"text-indent:0px;letter-spacing:normal;font-variant:normal;text-align:auto;font-style:normal;font-weight:normal;line-height:normal;border-collapse:separate;text-transform:none;font-size:medium;white-space:normal;font-family:Arial;word-spacing:0px\"><span style=\"font-family:&#39;Lucida Console&#39;;font-size:16px;line-height:19px;text-align:-webkit-left;white-space:pre-wrap\"></span></span><span style=\"text-indent:0px;letter-spacing:normal;font-variant:normal;text-align:auto;font-style:normal;font-weight:normal;line-height:normal;border-collapse:separate;text-transform:none;font-size:medium;white-space:normal;font-family:Arial;word-spacing:0px\"><span style=\"font-family:&#39;Lucida Console&#39;;font-size:16px;line-height:19px;text-align:-webkit-left;white-space:pre-wrap\"></span></span><span style=\"text-indent:0px;letter-spacing:normal;font-variant:normal;text-align:auto;font-style:normal;font-weight:normal;line-height:normal;border-collapse:separate;text-transform:none;font-size:medium;white-space:normal;font-family:Arial;word-spacing:0px\"><span style=\"font-family:&#39;Lucida Console&#39;;font-size:16px;line-height:19px;text-align:-webkit-left;white-space:pre-wrap\"></span></span></pre>\n\n</span></span></pre></span></span><span style=\"text-indent:0px;letter-spacing:normal;font-variant:normal;text-align:auto;font-style:normal;font-weight:normal;line-height:normal;border-collapse:separate;text-transform:none;font-size:medium;white-space:normal;font-family:Arial;word-spacing:0px\"><span style=\"font-family:&#39;Lucida Console&#39;;font-size:16px;line-height:19px;text-align:-webkit-left;white-space:pre-wrap\"><pre style=\"font-family:&#39;Lucida Console&#39;;font-size:12pt!important;outline-style:none;outline-width:initial;outline-color:initial;border-top-style:none;border-right-style:none;border-bottom-style:none;border-left-style:none;border-width:initial;border-color:initial;white-space:pre-wrap!important;margin-top:0px;margin-right:0px;margin-bottom:0px;margin-left:0px;line-height:1.2\">\n\n<span style=\"color:blue\">modelList.object@fits[poor.models</span><span style=\"text-indent:0px;letter-spacing:normal;font-variant:normal;text-align:auto;font-style:normal;font-weight:normal;line-height:normal;border-collapse:separate;text-transform:none;font-size:medium;white-space:normal;font-family:Arial;word-spacing:0px\"><span style=\"font-family:&#39;Lucida Console&#39;;font-size:16px;line-height:19px;text-align:-webkit-left;white-space:pre-wrap\"></span></span><span style=\"color:blue\">]&lt;-NULL<br>\n\n</span><br><font><span style=\"font-family:arial,sans-serif\">I&#39;m not entirely sure why you would do this, but this modified list could be used to generate new model-averaged predictions for just the subset of models.  I tried doing this to a small set of models and found that the predictions from a modelList where all but 1 model was removed were the same as when that single model itself was specified, yet the confidence intervals were different:<br>\n\n<br></span></font><span style=\"text-indent:0px;letter-spacing:normal;font-variant:normal;text-align:auto;font-style:normal;font-weight:normal;line-height:normal;border-collapse:separate;text-transform:none;font-size:medium;white-space:normal;font-family:Arial;word-spacing:0px\"><span style=\"font-family:&#39;Lucida Console&#39;;font-size:16px;line-height:19px;text-align:-webkit-left;white-space:pre-wrap\"><pre style=\"font-family:&#39;Lucida Console&#39;;font-size:12pt!important;outline-style:none;outline-width:initial;outline-color:initial;border-top-style:none;border-right-style:none;border-bottom-style:none;border-left-style:none;border-width:initial;border-color:initial;white-space:pre-wrap!important;margin-top:0px;margin-right:0px;margin-bottom:0px;margin-left:0px;line-height:1.2\">\n\n<span style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;color:blue\">&gt; </span><span style=\"color:blue\">predict(fm3, type=&quot;state&quot;, newdata=newDat)\n</span>  Predicted         SE     lower    upper\n1 0.8734059 0.08488826 0.6050754 0.968816\n<span style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;color:blue\">&gt; </span><span style=\"color:blue\">predict(modelList, type=&quot;state&quot;, newdata=newDat)\n</span>  Predicted         SE     lower    upper\n1 0.8734059 0.08488826 0.7070249 1.039787</pre></span></span><br><font><span style=\"font-family:arial,sans-serif\">Not sure what is going on there.  As for model-averaged coefficients, I recall reading that there are problems with trying to generate/interpret them.  I could be wrong.<span><font color=\"#888888\"><br>\n\n<br>-Dan</font></span></span></font> <br></pre></span></span></blockquote></div><br></div>"
